0056:     """
0057:     Move each marked cross object away from its marker to the grid edge while rotating the colored cross 180 degrees.
0058: 
0059:     Input structure:
0060:     - The background is the dominant color.
0061:     - Each 8-connected foreground object has nine pixels: a 4-pixel marker-color
0062:       sprite attached to a 5-pixel non-marker colored cross.
0063:     - Each object bbox is either 3x6 or 6x3, so the marker sprite is on exactly
0064:       one side of the cross.
0065: 
0066:     Rule:
0067:     - Move the whole object straight away from its marker side until the object
0068:       bbox touches the corresponding grid edge.
0069:     - Keep the marker sprite unchanged within the object.
0070:     - Rotate the 3x3 colored cross block by 180 degrees before placing it.
0071: 
0072:     Key insight:
0073:     The marker sprite is a directional tail; the cross is the leading payload,
0074:     and only that payload turns around during the slide to the edge.
